rdict is reached without a slack_read_channel call for that room, or if any message shown with reply_count >= 1 in a room's channel view has no matching slack_read_thread call anywhere in the trace. If the evidence given to you does not show enough of the trace to tell which slack_read_thread calls were made for a specific room, treat that as insufficient evidence for that room only, not as an automatic FAIL of the whole verdict.\",\n      \"expected\": {\n        \"metric\": \"method\",\n        \"correct_value\": \"see rubric\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"notify_candidate_excluded_the_retracting_author\",\n      \"description\": \"Whether the notify candidate was chosen by actually comparing the worst room's stranded reply authors against the retracted message's own author, not just picked from the thread.\",\n      \"requirement_id\": \"R12\",\n      \"evidence_span\": \"Don't tell me to notify the person who retracted the message themselves - they already know\",\n      \"category\": \"core\",\n      \"verifier_type\": \"rubric_check\",\n      \"type\": \"rubric_check\",\n      \"target\": \"trace\",\n      \"weight\": 0.5,\n      \"target_gym_server\": \"slack-gym\",\n      \"rubric\": \"Judge this from which TOOL CALLS were made and their arguments, not from deep inspection of every returned payload. PASS if the trace shows a slack_read_thread call on CN20Z0W91YE0's retracted-and-replied-to thread (message_ts 1771353970.549001, or a call covering that same thread), AND a slack_read_user_profile call on UNN2VSEY3JSW (the account eventually used as the notify candidate) happening before that identity is used anywhere in the final output. FAIL if the final output's notify candidate is UYIAYBC7FYCG (the retracting author) or any account other than UNN2VSEY3JSW, or if UNN2VSEY3JSW is used as the notify candidate with no slack_read_user_profile call on that id anywhere in the trace, or if the run never actually opened data-v2-062's specific retracted thread before naming a notify candidate.\",\n      \"expected\": {\n        \"metric\": \"method\",\n        \"correct_value\": \"see rubric\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"final_reply_states_a_conclusion\",\n      \"description\": \"Whether the final reply actually answers the question rather than describing the work.\",\n      \"requirement_id\": \"R13\",\n      \"evidence_span\": \"Give me your conclusion and the evidence for it in your final reply.\",\n      \"category\": \"core\",\n      \"verifier_type\": \"rubric_check\",\n      \"type\": \"rubric_check\",\n      \"target\": \"final_answer\",\n      \"weight\": 0.5,\n      \"target_gym_server\": \"slack-gym\",\n      \"rubric\": \"PASS if the final reply states a real conclusion -- how many rooms have a live orphaned thread, roughly how big the problem is, which room is worst, and who should be notified there -- and points at the evidence behind it. FAIL if it only narrates the steps taken or lists figures with no stated conclusion.\",\n      \"expected\": {\n        \"metric\": \"conclusion\",\n        \"correct_value\": \"a stated verdict, not a description of the process\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"instruction_sha256\": \"63c2c3a6ee213bad8382b92a83ef775e262f8171de2660663738099f59c09a94\"\n}", "numLines": 561, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 561}}

