{
  "layer1_package_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "task.toml, instruction.md, solution/ (solve.sh, solve.py, golden_trajectory.json 45 steps, write_artifacts.py + artifact_plan.json, final_answer.md, emit_oracle_trajectory.py), tests/ (manifest.json 16 verifier_configs, test.sh -> test_gvs.sh -> test_outputs.py + verifier_engine.py + vendored rl_world_verifiers) and environment/ (Dockerfile, entrypoint.sh, proxy) jointly describe one executable, gradable task. manifest.instruction_sha256 63c2c3a6... equals the sha256 of instruction.md, and environment/_app/ is byte-identical to task.toml/instruction.md/tests (verified by diff -r). All mandatory subchecks pass."
  },
  "layer1_package_consistency__cross_artifact_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "No source is missing. Deliverable paths (/workspace/metrics.json, /workspace/orphaned_thread_audit.csv), the gym write-back into CN20Z0W91YE0, and the final reply are all produced by solution/ and read by tests/manifest.json. The gym data is served by the pinned image (company-synthetic-20260910-1150-pt-main) via the proxy at localhost:7000 declared in [[environment.mcp_servers]]; no separate input fixtures are declared or needed (tests/task_inputs.py is unused template code, and file_check explicitly refuses specs that read seeded inputs)."
  },
  "layer1_package_consistency__instruction_verifier_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Every reward-bearing check traces to instruction text: R1/R2/R3/R4 -> the six metrics.json keys the prompt pins; R5 -> 'exactly these columns in this order' + 'List every room that has this problem'; R6 -> per-row cell values; R7/R9 -> 'post one message - in the single worst room only, nowhere else'; R8 -> 'end the message with exactly these two lines'; R11 -> 'you have to actually open every thread with a reply and look'; R12 -> 'Don't tell me to notify the person who retracted the message themselves'; R13 -> 'Give me your conclusion and the evidence for it'. R0 (>=10 gym calls) is a floor implied by the mandated per-thread walk. The only near-verifier-only item is R10 (86 messages across the six rooms = 85 seed + 1), a do-no-harm side-effect gate no correct solve can trip. No material instruction requirement is ungraded (only the free-form body of the posted message beyond the two pinned lines is unscored)."
  },
  "layer1_package_consistency__solution_instruction_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "solution/ produces every requested deliverable: write_artifacts.py materialises metrics.json with exactly the six pinned keys (numbers as numbers, ids/names as strings) and orphaned_thread_audit.csv with the five pinned columns and four rows; golden_trajectory.json step s45 posts one slack_send_message into CN20Z0W91YE0 ending 'orphaned: 4\\nnotify: Mitali Naidu'; final_answer.md states the conclusion and evidence. The derivation uses only tool-reachable facts (deleted_ts on thread-root messages, reply_count, slack_read_user_profile real_name) — confirmed against the replayed tool payloads in evaluations/oracle/verifier/golden_trajectory.json."
  },
  "layer1_package_consistency__solution_verifier_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "solve.sh stages the oracle's deliverables into /workspace (the exact directory _run_file_check grades) and emits an ATIF trace to /logs/agent/trajectory.json so the trace/tool_execution verifiers see the replay; test_outputs.py additionally falls back to the augmented golden only for agent name 'oracle'. Checked-in evidence (evaluations/oracle/verifier/verifier_summary.json) shows all 16 verifiers pass on the golden with no shortcut: each check fired on its own evidence (file_check rewards 1.0, database_state actual==expected, three rubric_check verdicts with substantive motivations)."
  },
  "layer1_package_consistency__manifest_environment_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Dockerfile FROM matches metadata.mcp_servers_extended.image; healthcheck curls the same :7000 the [[environment.mcp_servers]] URL uses; WORKDIR /workspace matches the instruction's deliverable paths and _run_file_check's default; TASK_DIR=/app matches test_gvs.sh and TASK_DIR in test_outputs.py; /app is chmod go-rwx with agent user rlgymagent as declared in [agent].user; environment/_app mirror is byte-identical to the task root. state_snapshot_enabled=false is consistent with the engine-owned scoring path (state/sql weights 0.0, allowed_verifier_types = rubric + agentic_llm_as_judge). tests/test_requirements.txt only pins litellm while the vendored verifiers also need pydantic/jsonpath_ng/tenacity, but the checked-in oracle verification ran those code paths successfully in this image, so the declaration gap is not contradictory in practice."
  },
  "layer1_package_consistency__declared_executed_verifier_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "test.sh runs test_gvs.sh which execs tests/test_outputs.py; with allowed_verifier_types containing 'agentic_llm_as_judge' the engine path (_emit_engine_owned_reward -> score_benchmark_verifiers -> run_benchmark_verifiers) is the sole scorer and consumes manifest.verifier_configs. All 16 declared verifiers appear in the oracle's verification_results with total=16, unscored=0. rubric.toml carries only a system preamble (no criteria items), so it contributes zero verifiers — declared but inert, and it is not represented as coverage. No executable reward-bearing check exists outside the declarations."
  },
  "layer1_package_consistency__artifact_contract_consistency": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Instruction names /workspace/metrics.json and /workspace/orphaned_thread_audit.csv; verifier_specs read the same relative names under the resolved workspace (/workspace, overridable via TH_WORKSPACE_DIR, failing loudly if absent). The connector-side surface (one new message in CN20Z0W91YE0 by UVS1ZHNER2I5) is graded from the live gym DB, the same surface slack_send_message writes. No filename, path or output-surface drift between produced and graded submission."
  },
  "layer1_clarity_scope": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "All four clarity subchecks pass: output surfaces, representation rules, and the process requirements the verifier grades are each stated in instruction.md, and the prompt is clean, unredacted prose. The vendor's own reader study (consistency/readers.json) shows independent readers recovering the exact deliverable shape and field semantics."
  },
  "layer1_clarity_scope__output_surface_contract": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Graded surfaces are exactly the instructed ones: two workspace files (pinned by path and key/column name), one Slack message in the single worst room ending with two pinned lines, and a final reply containing the conclusion. Nothing is graded on a location the instruction does not require; the do-no-harm state check (R10, seed messages intact) is a side-effect guard on the same write-back the instruction scopes to one room."
  },
  "layer1_clarity_scope__representation_contract": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The prompt pins the key names, that numbers are 'plain numbers' and identifiers 'plain strings', the CSV column names and order, and the exact two trailing lines. Free choices are genuinely free in the verifier: metrics.json key order/nesting/pretty-printing (recursive-descent $.. paths), CSV row order/quoting/whitespace/letter case (explicitly freed in the rubric), and SQL LIKE that strips spaces and is case-insensitive. consistency/mutations.json records cosmetic mutants (reordered keys, int-as-float, extra key, wrapped-in-object, reordered rows) all passing."
  },
  "layer1_clarity_scope__process_requirement_disclosure": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The two trace-graded rubrics correspond to explicitly stated work. R11 ('a slack_read_thread for every message with reply_count >= 1 in each of the six rooms') restates 'you have to actually open every thread with a reply and look'. R12 requires opening data-v2-062's retracted thread and a profile read on UNN2VSEY3JSW before naming them; the thread payload only exposes the handle ('Mii'), and the real name 'Mitali Naidu' comes only from slack_read_user_profile (verified in the replayed payloads), so the profile call is a necessary consequence of the instructed answer, not an extra workflow. R0's floor of 10 gym calls cannot bind a legitimate run."
  },
  "layer1_clarity_scope__redaction_readability": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "instruction.md contains no placeholders, elisions or broken grammar. Identities (six named rooms), relationships (retracting author vs reply author) and the exclusion rule ('Don't tell me to notify the person who retracted the message themselves') are stated plainly."
  },
  "layer1_realism_leakage": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Domain model, references, workflow realism and golden isolation all hold; no subcheck fails."
  },
  "layer1_realism_leakage__domain_correctness": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The Slack mechanics are coherent with the served gym: deleted_ts is a per-message metadata flag, reply_count carries the stranded count, and real names require slack_read_user_profile. I recomputed the gold from the replayed tool payloads in evaluations/oracle/verifier/golden_trajectory.json: 27 threads with reply_count>=1 across six rooms (4+7+4+6+4+2), the data-v2-062 root ts 1771353970.549001 by UYIAYBC7FYCG carries deleted_ts with replies from UNN2VSEY3JSW and UYIAYBC7FYCG, and UNN2VSEY3JSW's profile real_name is 'Mitali Naidu' — consistent with 4 rooms / 5 stranded replies / worst CN20Z0W91YE0 (2) / notify UNN2VSEY3JSW. One inaccurate author-side note in task.toml metadata ('the channel view returns it too') — the replayed slack_read_channel payloads do not include deleted_ts — but it is grader-only prose that errs toward requiring more work, and the agent-facing instruction correctly says the flag is only visible on the message record."
  },
  "layer1_realism_leakage__authoritative_reference_validity": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "No external laws/standards are cited. The only authority is the pinned dataset image and the gym's own records; task.toml documents the SQL used against the grounding DB and states the values were re-read through the served gym, which the checked-in oracle replay corroborates tool-call by tool-call."
  },
  "layer1_realism_leakage__workflow_realism": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "A data-governance retraction audit across six rooms the acting identity belongs to, with a sized problem, a worst room, a notify candidate and a single flagging write-back, is a plausible real request with real user value. Decoys (an inert no-reply retraction, a self-reply) are natural data conditions, not contrived traps, and every needed fact is reachable through the 14 allowlisted Slack tools."
  },
  "layer1_realism_leakage__golden_isolation": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The image copies only task.toml, instruction.md and tests/ into /app and then chmod -R go-rwx /app; the agent runs as rlgymagent with only /workspace writable, and solution/ is never copied into the image. The gold values live in task.toml (root-only). entrypoint.sh's env dump to agent-readable /logs redacts the access token and prints only the mcp_servers_extended block, not the GOLD section. The proxy's /raw/{name}/state SQL route is gated behind a per-boot secret at root-only /app/.raw_state_secret, and /raw/{name}/step enforces the same allowed_tools list as the MCP path."
  },
  "layer2_difficulty": {
    "outcome": "fail",
    "explanation": "evaluations/ contains only evaluations/oracle (one oracle trial: config.json/lock.json/result.json with agent.name='oracle', trajectory, verifier outputs). There are zero GLM 5.2 model attempts, so the required four eligible trajectory/result pairs, their provenance and the strict-pass distribution cannot be established. This is missing evidence, not evidence of an easy task."
  },
  "layer2_difficulty__evidence_pairing_count": {
    "outcome": "fail",
    "explanation": "Only one attempt directory exists (evaluations/oracle) and it is the oracle replay, not a model rollout. Zero of the four claimed/expected eligible attempts are present, so pairing, duplication and orphan checks cannot be satisfied."
  },
  "layer2_difficulty__provenance_validity": {
    "outcome": "fail",
    "explanation": "The only provenance in evaluations/ (oracle/config.json, oracle/lock.json, oracle/result.json) records agent.name='oracle', model_name=null and agent_info.model_info=null. Nothing establishes four independent GLM 5.2 attempts; the only GLM 5.2 reference is the verifier's JUDGE_MODEL (openai/glm-5.2), which is the judge, not the solving model."
  },
  "layer2_difficulty__strict_pass_distribution": {
    "outcome": "fail",
    "explanation": "Zero eligible (non-oracle) attempts exist, so the required 'exactly four eligible attempts, at most two at reward exactly 1.0' cannot hold. The single recorded reward, {\"reward\": 1.0} in oracle/result.json and verifier/reward.txt, belongs to the oracle replay and is ineligible."
  },
  "layer2_difficulty__failure_cause_validity": {
    "outcome": "fail",
    "explanation": "No model failures are recorded in evaluations/, so no failure cause can be attributed to task difficulty rather than defects. Missing evidence."
  },
  "layer2_solvability": {
    "outcome": "fail",
    "explanation": "No non-oracle trajectory/result pair exists in evaluations/. The only reward of exactly 1.0 comes from the oracle replay of solution/golden_trajectory.json (agent 'oracle', trial slack-4__fYHZHen), which is solution-replay evidence and cannot demonstrate solvability by an eligible agent."
  },
  "layer2_solvability__eligible_strict_pass": {
    "outcome": "fail",
    "explanation": "The single strict pass (reward 1.0, core_passed true, 16/16 verifiers) is evaluations/oracle — an oracle/solution replay. No eligible agent run earning 1.0 is saved."
